    <!-- Introduction 1 -->
    <string name="introduction_1_title">Sleep cycles, what are they?</string>
    <string name="introduction_1_body_1">When you sleep, your brain cycles through loops. One full loop takes about 90 minutes and is called a sleep cycle</string>
    <string name="introduction_1_body_2">A full, refreshing night typically includes 4 to 6 cycles, which adds up to 6 to 9 hours of sleep</string>
    <string name="introduction_1_body_3">Waking up between cycles feels natural and refreshing. Waking up during one causes that heavy, disoriented feeling known as sleep inertia</string>
    <string name="introduction_1_body_4">Cyclo helps you avoid that by finding the best times to fall asleep or wake up, always aligned with the end of a cycle</string>

